<article class="env-lemma" id="0FQL">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0FQL">Lemma <span data-tag="0FQL">22.28.5</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a ring. Let $(A, \text{d})$ and $(B, \text{d})$ be differential graded $R$-algebras. Let $P$ be a differential graded $(A, B)$-bimodule having property (P) with corresponding filtration $F_\bullet $, then we obtain a short exact sequence </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  0 \to \bigoplus \nolimits F_ iP \to \bigoplus \nolimits F_ iP \to P \to 0  \]
</div>
  <p> of differential graded $(A, B)$-bimodules which is split as a sequence of graded $(A, B)$-bimodules. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Immediate from Lemmas <a href="/tag/0FQJ" data-tag="0FQJ">22.28.3</a> and <a href="/tag/09KL" data-tag="09KL">22.20.1</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>